 "purpose": "MEASUREMENT ONLY. Quantify two memo performance bugs in the repo-verbatim certificate extractor class4_child1_cert_extractor_exact.ts (git blob 52bcaf50...) - the certificate-extractor copy of the defects repaired in the v15->v16 runner (2026-11-14) - and measure fixed variants on the published cost-73k WIN7-D10 band. Bug A: memo key arrays mK0..mK3 are Uint32Array while the comparison operands M0..M3 are int32, so positions on cells 31/63/95 (bit 31 of words 0/1/2) never match in memoFind and memoEntry re-inserts them on every visit (up to 64 copies = the key's whole 64-slot probe window). Bug B: the no-win/no-lose negative-bound updates compare against the 255 sentinel in the wrong direction and never fire (nowin=nolose stay 255; both memoFind negative-bound shortcuts dead). Both bugs are performance-only (memo is an optimization): every published certificate, node count and verdict remains valid, and both fixed variants re-extract all 22 published certificates byte-identically (hard gate, split files concatenated).",
